---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import OrgCards from '../components/OrgCards.astro'
import { href, ISO_7372_URL, UNECE_UNTDED_URL, tc154ResolutionUrl } from '../lib/site'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — UN/TDED"
  description="The status of this website as a member-contribution pilot project, the ISO/TC 154 mandate behind it, and the two organizations that publish the United Nations Trade Data Elements Directory."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-un-deep">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-mono text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
      UN<span class="name-slash">/</span>TDED
    </h1>

    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 font-serif text-xl text-body">
      <span><strong class="text-ink">UN</strong> — United Nations</span>
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-mono text-un">/</span>
      <span><strong class="text-ink">TDED</strong> — Trade Data Elements Directory</span>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Mission</h2>
      <p class="prose-def mt-3">
        The United Nations Trade Data Elements Directory (UNTDED) is the
        controlled vocabulary that defines every data element on an aligned
        trade document, with its number, name, definition and representation.
        This website publishes the 2005 edition, which is ECE/TRADE/362 and
        ISO 7372:2005, as an open and machine-readable dataset, so that this
        vocabulary can be maintained and consumed as data rather than as a
        scanned PDF.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      id="pilot"
      class="mt-10 rounded-md border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-6 dark:border-amber-800/60 dark:bg-amber-950/40"
    >
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Pilot status</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
        This website and the machine-readable dataset that it publishes are a{' '}
        <strong class="text-ink">member contribution and a pilot project</strong> to the
        United Nations Economic Commission for Europe (UNECE), through UN/CEFACT, and
        to ISO/TC 154. The work is performed to complement the two organizations and is
        recorded in JWG 9 resolution P-2026-07 (see{' '}
        <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href="#mandate">the mandate</a>).
        The website is <strong class="text-ink">not an official project or publication</strong>{' '}
        of either organization, and <strong class="text-ink">neither organization has endorsed it</strong>.
        The data is digitized from the printed edition and is provided without any
        guarantee of accuracy, so use of the website is at the user’s own risk. The
        UN/TDED publication itself is the official publication ECE/TRADE/362, published
        in parallel as ISO 7372:2005. The official sources remain the publications of
        the two organizations:{' '}
        <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={UNECE_UNTDED_URL}>UN/TDED — UNECE</a> and{' '}
        <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={ISO_7372_URL}>ISO 7372 — ISO</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Name and colours</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] sm:items-center">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-line bg-mist p-5">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center border-l-4 border-un bg-paper px-4 py-2 font-mono text-3xl tabular-nums text-ink">1001</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">UN<span class="name-slash">/</span>TDED</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <span class="mt-1 inline-block h-3 w-3 shrink-0 rounded-[2px] bg-un" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span>The slash and the accents use <strong class="text-ink">UN blue #009EDB</strong>,
            which is the official blue of the United Nations (Pantone 2925).</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <span class="mt-1 inline-flex shrink-0 gap-1" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="inline-block h-3 w-3 rounded-[2px] bg-flag"></span>
              <span class="inline-block h-3 w-3 rounded-[2px] bg-cat-5"></span>
            </span>
            <span>The <strong class="text-ink">category colours</strong> assign one colour to
            each tag range, in tag order.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <span class="mt-1 inline-block h-3 w-3 shrink-0 rounded-[2px] border border-line bg-paper" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span>The <strong class="text-ink">name</strong> follows the spelling convention of
            the UN standards family, which includes UN/CEFACT and UN/EDIFACT.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <span class="mt-1 inline-block h-3 w-3 shrink-0 rounded-[2px] border border-line bg-mist" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span>The <strong class="text-ink">tag plate</strong> reproduces the bordered plate
            with the four-digit tag that follows the pre-printed field boxes of trade
            documents.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Operation and governance</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-body">
        This website and its repositories are a pilot project performed to complement
        the work of the United Nations and the International Organization for
        Standardization, which jointly maintain ISO 7372 and the TDED through{' '}
        <strong class="text-ink">ISO/TC 154/JWG 9</strong>. The website is not an official
        project of either organization, as the{' '}
        <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href="#pilot">pilot status</a>{' '}
        above states.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-5">
        <OrgCards />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="mandate" class="mt-10 rounded-md border border-line bg-mist p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">The mandate</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body">
        The work is mandated by <strong class="text-ink">
        <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={tc154ResolutionUrl('P-2026-07')}>ISO/TC 154 document
        N1727</a></strong>, which records the resolutions of the 45th plenary meeting of
        ISO/TC 154, held at DIN in Berlin on 2026-08-31 and 2026-09-04. All resolutions
        were approved by the six participating members: DIN, SAC, BSI, JISC, UNI and KATS.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="mt-4 border-l-4 border-un bg-paper p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink">
        <p class="font-semibold">
          <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={tc154ResolutionUrl('P-2026-07')}>
            Resolution P-2026-07 (JWG 9)
          </a>{' '}
          — Encouragement for exploring the use of an
          open-source platform to support the maintenance and publication of ISO 7372
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-body">
          "ISO/TC154 resolve to explore the use of an open-source platform (such
          as the pilot UN Gitlab environment) to support the maintenance and
          publication of ISO 7372. ISO/TC 154 also request that ISO Central
          Secretariat can share best practices on OSD and Smart Standards
          developed that could support this work."
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
        Two companion resolutions apply.{' '}
        <a class="font-semibold text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={tc154ResolutionUrl('P-2026-06')}>P-2026-06</a>{' '}
        (JWG 9) calls for strengthened expert support on the ISO side and on the UNECE
        side for the timely publication of ISO 7372 before October 2028.{' '}
        <a class="font-semibold text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={tc154ResolutionUrl('P-2026-01')}>P-2026-01</a>
        {' '}(JWG 1) initiates a meeting with the UNECE Secretariat on the stalled
        maintenance and publication of the UN/EDIFACT Directories, whose D.25A release
        is severely delayed. This platform, which comprises the dataset, this website
        and the source code, is the open-source platform that those resolutions call
        for. It is developed and operated as a pilot project to ISO/TC 154 and UNECE,
        with UNTDED 2005 as its first complete edition.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Licensing and attribution</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
        The content of the directory is the UN publication <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={UNECE_UNTDED_URL}>ECE/TRADE/362</a> (in parallel
        as <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={ISO_7372_URL}>ISO 7372:2005</a>), © United Nations / UNECE, and it is reproduced with
        attribution. The code and this website are open source under the MIT license.
        The <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={href('/download')}>download page</a>{' '}
        lists the exact artifacts.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
